diff --git a/CHANGES.md b/CHANGES.md
index 3efb850..717f619 100644
--- a/CHANGES.md
+++ b/CHANGES.md
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 
 Unreleased
 
+- Add the `suffixes` parameter to {class}`Path`, which only accepts paths that end
+  with one of the given extensions, compared case-insensitively.
 - Drop support for Python 3.10. {pr}`3920` {pr}`3921`
 - A parameter name that is not a valid Python identifier, or that is a Python
   keyword, is deprecated and raises `TypeError` in Click 9.0. {pr}`3866`
diff --git a/docs/handling-files.md b/docs/handling-files.md
index 261ce8a..847a698 100644
--- a/docs/handling-files.md
+++ b/docs/handling-files.md
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@ For handling paths, the {class}`Path` type is better than a `str`. Some notable
 - The `exists` argument will verify whether the path exists.
 - `readable`, `writable`, and `executable` can perform permission checks.
 - `file_okay` and `dir_okay` allow specifying whether files/directories are accepted.
+- `suffixes` restricts the accepted file extensions, ignoring case, for example `suffixes=[".csv", ".tsv"]`.
 - Error messages are nicely formatted using {func}`format_filename` so any undecodable bytes will be printed nicely.
 
 See {class}`Path` for all features.
